Seam: chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, source_set("core") — the target
      chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc actually builds
      in, not //chrome/browser/ui.
Why: GN wiring for patch 0150. The hook includes an //arcium/ui/browser
     header and //chrome/browser:core has no Arcium dep of its own, so
     `gn check` rejects the include even though ninja accepts it. `gn check`
     on that target is what says whether this is still needed after a
     rebase.

     No cycle: `gn check --root=/Volumes/Texternal/chromium/src
     /Volumes/Texternal/chromium/src/out/dev "//chrome/browser:core"` prints
     `Header dependency check OK` with this dep added, and //arcium/ui/browser
     depends on nothing that reaches back into //chrome/browser:core.

     Patch 0010's dependency does not transit here. //chrome/browser/ui:ui
     already depends on //arcium/ui/browser (patch 0010), but that dep is a
     private `deps` entry, not a `public_dep`, so it stops at
     //chrome/browser/ui:ui and never reaches //chrome/browser:core. Making
     patch 0010's dependency public instead was tried and rejected: it lands
     inside patch 0010's hunk context, which breaks 0010's already-applied
     check and makes scripts/sync non-idempotent — the same reason patch
     0125 gives for not touching chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn a second time.
Delegates to: nothing. GN wiring carries no call.

